{
  "full_prompt_html": "<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 9pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52);\">Act as an internal communications director, a change management consultant and an editor who writes for busy readers.</span></p>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 9pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52);\">We need to announce a change that some staff will not welcome. Draft the announcement and the plan around it. [Describe the change, the reason for it, the date it takes effect and who it affects.] [Paste any questions or concerns staff have already raised.]</span></p>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 9pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52);\">Prepare the communication in four parts:</span></p>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 6pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(34, 31, 31);\"><b>1. Audience and Impact</b></span></p>\n<ul data-editing-info=\"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}\" style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; list-style-type: disc;\">\n<li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nIdentify each group affected and state what changes for them in practical terms: their tasks, tools, schedule or pay.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nPredict the main concern of each group and how strongly they will feel it.</div>\n</li></ul>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 6pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(34, 31, 31);\"><b>2. The Announcement</b></span></p>\n<ul data-editing-info=\"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}\" style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; list-style-type: disc;\">\n<li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nDraft an email of no more than 250 words. State the change in the first sentence, then the reason, then what happens next.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nExplain the reason in business terms that staff can check, not in slogans.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nSay plainly what is not changing and what is still undecided. Do not use words such as “exciting”, “journey” or “transformation”.</div>\n</li></ul>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 6pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(34, 31, 31);\"><b>3. Questions and Answers</b></span></p>\n<ul data-editing-info=\"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}\" style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; list-style-type: disc;\">\n<li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nWrite the ten questions staff are most likely to ask, including the uncomfortable ones, with a direct answer to each.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nWhere an answer is not yet known, say so and give the date when it will be.</div>\n</li></ul>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 6pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(34, 31, 31);\"><b>4. Sequence and Channels</b></span></p>\n<ul data-editing-info=\"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}\" style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; list-style-type: disc;\">\n<li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nRecommend who hears first, such as managers before their teams, and how far in advance.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nGive managers a five-point briefing so they answer questions consistently.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nSuggest how to collect feedback in the first two weeks, for example a Teams channel or a short Microsoft Forms survey.</div>\n</li></ul>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 9pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52);\">Deliver the announcement email, the question-and-answer list, the manager briefing, and a timeline with one line for each step of the rollout.</span></p>",
  "n": 10,
  "subject_area": "Marketing and comms",
  "summary": "Draft an internal announcement for an unwelcome change, with audience impact, a plain-language email, honest answers, manager briefing, and rollout sequence.",
  "title": "Draft an internal announcement for an unwelcome change"
}
